# Notes API

A simple REST API for creating and viewing notes, built with FastAPI.

## Features

- Get all notes
- Create a new note
- Get a note by ID
- Returns `404` if a note is not found

## Tech Stack

- Python 3.10+
- FastAPI
- Pydantic

## Installation

```bash
git clone [https://github.com/username/notes-api.git](https://github.com/username/notes-api.git)
cd notes-api
python -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate  # Windows: venv\Scripts\activate
pip install fastapi uvicorn
```

## Running the App

```bash
uvicorn main:app --reload
```

The API will be available at:

```text
http://127.0.0.1:8000
```

Interactive Swagger documentation:

```text
http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs
```

## Endpoints

| Method | Endpoint | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `GET` | `/notes` | Get all notes |
| `POST` | `/notes` | Create a new note |
| `GET` | `/notes/{note_id}` | Get a note by ID |

## Example Request

### Create a Note

```bash
curl -X POST "http://127.0.0.1:8000/notes" \
-H "Content-Type: application/json"